    "question": {
      ":question/id": "a6884e5a-a3cb-544b-b94b-b4d350473e04",
      ":question/problem": "Express $\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)$ in terms of $\\sin x$ and $\\cos x$. Enter the signed coefficients.\n\n$\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)=$ {{field-1}} $\\sin x\\,+$ {{field-2}} $\\cos x$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Use the difference formula:\n\n$$\n\\cos(u-v)=\\cos u\\cos v+\\sin u\\sin v\n$$\n\nWith $u=x$ and $v=\\frac{7\\pi}{4}$, the exact values are $\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ and $\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$. Substitute and collect the terms in the requested order:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos\\left(x-\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)&=\\cos x\\cos\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)+\\sin x\\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{4}\\right)\\\\\n&=\\cos x\\cdot\\left(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)+\\sin x\\cdot\\left(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\right)\\\\\n&=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\sin x+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cos x.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
